# Watches this boot until the login screen (greetd's greeter) or a desktop has
# been up for a while, then marks the boot good: the boot try counter on the
# EFI partition is cleared and the newest snapshot recorded as the last good
# one (`ribbon rollback`'s default). After an update (the counter is armed) a
# boot that gets nowhere within BOOT_GOOD_TIMEOUT restarts the machine, and the
# initramfs falls back to the pre-update snapshot once the tries are used up
# (docs/SYSTEM-UPDATES.md 5.5, 7.8). It starts as soon as the filesystems are
# mounted and does not wait for loginready or greetd on purpose: a boot that
# hangs before the login screen must still be counted.
type = process
command = /usr/bin/ribbon-snapshot boot-watch
restart = false
log-type = buffer
depends-on: early-filesystems
